\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Phone menu:
\f0\b0  it opens as floating white panels over the page, with no dark overlay. The burger tumbles as it turns into a cross. The menu rows rise one after another, 50ms apart, on a slightly bouncy curve. The contact row finishes with a yellow circle holding a face that pops in. The whole opening takes 800ms, and closing reverses everything at once. I confirmed these timings on real open and close clicks.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 "Which decision is in front of you?":
\f0\b0  this section is on the Strategy page, not the home page. It has ten near-square white cards, five across on desktop and full-width rows on phones. They fade up with a 50ms stagger, lift 4px on hover, and each opens a panel on the same page that loads its content from the detail page. The spec maps it to hurulab's nine services.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Color blocks:
\f0\b0  every section is a rounded slab with no divider lines. The home page opens with green, runs through long beige stretches, returns to green for the call to action and closes on a yellow footer. Each inner page has its own hero color.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Banned patterns found:
\f0\b0 \strokec2  the "Brands that choose MindMarket" logo scroller, the frosted blur behind the decision panels, and uppercase labels above headings. There is also a "Most chosen" badge, a face in the "Get a quote" button that follows the mouse, and an emoji on the contact page. All are marked "do not copy".\

\f2\b \strokec2 Loader:
\f0\b0 \strokec2  a desktop-only loader draws the logo, then lifts like a curtain about 2.25s after the page's scripts start running. It hides nothing that needs loading; it only stages the entrance. Behind the animated characters, the heaviest downloads are a 660KB animation engine plus 14 character files totaling 312KB.\

